{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Chain Rule & Automatic Differentiation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: The Value class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Value:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data, children=(), op=''):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.data = data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._backward = lambda: None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._prev = set(children)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._op = op"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __repr__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return f\"Value(data={self.data:.4f}, grad={self.grad:.4f})\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every `Value` stores its numeric data, its gradient (initially zero), a backward function, and pointers to child nodes that produced it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Arithmetic operations with gradient tracking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __add__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        other = other if isinstance(other, Value) else Value(other)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(self.data + other.data, (self, other), '+')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            other.grad += out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __mul__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        other = other if isinstance(other, Value) else Value(other)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(self.data * other.data, (self, other), '*')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += other.data * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            other.grad += self.data * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def relu(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(max(0, self.data), (self,), 'relu')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += (1.0 if out.data > 0 else 0.0) * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each operation creates a closure that knows how to compute local gradients and multiply by the upstream gradient (`out.grad`). The `+=` handles the case where a value is used in multiple operations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: The backward pass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        topo = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        visited = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def build_topo(v):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if v not in visited:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                visited.add(v)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for child in v._prev:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    build_topo(child)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                topo.append(v)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        build_topo(self)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.grad = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for v in reversed(topo):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v._backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Topological sort ensures every node's gradient is fully computed before it propagates to its children. The seed gradient is 1.0 (dy/dy = 1)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: More operations for a complete engine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The basic Value class handles addition, multiplication, and relu. A real autograd engine needs more. Here are the operations you need to build neural networks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __neg__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self * -1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __sub__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self + (-other)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __radd__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self + other"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __rmul__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self * other"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __rsub__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return other + (-self)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __pow__(self, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(self.data ** n, (self,), f'**{n}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += n * (self.data ** (n - 1)) * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __truediv__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self * (other ** -1) if isinstance(other, Value) else self * (Value(other) ** -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def exp(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        e = math.exp(self.data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(e, (self,), 'exp')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += e * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def log(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(math.log(self.data), (self,), 'log')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += (1.0 / self.data) * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def tanh(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t = math.tanh(self.data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = Value(t, (self,), 'tanh')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        def _backward():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.grad += (1 - t ** 2) * out.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out._backward = _backward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Why each operation matters:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Operation | Backward rule | Used in |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----------|--------------|---------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `__sub__` | Reuses add + neg | Loss computation (pred - target) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `__pow__` | n * x^(n-1) | Polynomial activations, MSE (error^2) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `__truediv__` | Reuses mul + pow(-1) | Normalization, learning rate scaling |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `exp` | exp(x) * upstream | Softmax, log-likelihood |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `log` | (1/x) * upstream | Cross-entropy loss, log probabilities |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `tanh` | (1 - tanh^2) * upstream | Classic activation function |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The clever part: `__sub__` and `__truediv__` are defined in terms of existing operations. They get correct gradients for free because the chain rule composes through the underlying add/mul/pow operations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Mini MLP from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "With a complete Value class, you can build a neural network. No PyTorch. No NumPy. Just Values and the chain rule."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Neuron:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_inputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w = [Value(random.uniform(-1, 1)) for _ in range(n_inputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b = Value(0.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        act = sum((wi * xi for wi, xi in zip(self.w, x)), self.b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return act.tanh()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.w + [self.b]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Layer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_inputs, n_outputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.neurons = [Neuron(n_inputs) for _ in range(n_outputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [n(x) for n in self.neurons]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [p for n in self.neurons for p in n.parameters()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class MLP:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, sizes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layers = [Layer(sizes[i], sizes[i+1]) for i in range(len(sizes)-1)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __call__(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for layer in self.layers:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = layer(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x[0] if len(x) == 1 else x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def parameters(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [p for layer in self.layers for p in layer.parameters()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A `Neuron` computes `tanh(w1*x1 + w2*x2 + ... + b)`. A `Layer` is a list of neurons. An `MLP` stacks layers. Every weight is a `Value`, so calling `loss.backward()` propagates gradients to every parameter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Training on XOR:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = MLP([2, 4, 1])  # 2 inputs, 4 hidden neurons, 1 output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "xs = [[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ys = [-1, 1, 1, -1]  # XOR pattern (using -1/1 for tanh)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preds = [model(x) for x in xs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = sum((p - y) ** 2 for p, y in zip(preds, ys))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in model.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p.grad = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lr = 0.05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p in model.parameters():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p.data -= lr * p.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step % 20 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"step {step:3d}  loss = {loss.data:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\nPredictions after training:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for x, y in zip(xs, ys):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  input={x}  target={y:2d}  pred={model(x).data:6.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is micrograd. A complete neural network training loop in pure Python with automatic differentiation. Every commercial deep learning framework does the same thing at massive scale."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Gradient checking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "How do you know your autodiff is correct? Compare it against numerical derivatives. This is gradient checking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gradient_check(build_expr, x_val, h=1e-7):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = Value(x_val)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = build_expr(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    autodiff_grad = x.grad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y_plus = build_expr(Value(x_val + h)).data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y_minus = build_expr(Value(x_val - h)).data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    numerical_grad = (y_plus - y_minus) / (2 * h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    diff = abs(autodiff_grad - numerical_grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return autodiff_grad, numerical_grad, diff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Test it on a complex expression:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def expr(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return (x ** 3 + x * 2 + 1).tanh()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ad, num, diff = gradient_check(expr, 0.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Autodiff:  {ad:.8f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Numerical: {num:.8f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Difference: {diff:.2e}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Difference should be < 1e-5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Gradient checking is essential when implementing new operations. If your backward pass has a bug, the numerical check catches it. Every serious deep learning implementation runs gradient checks during development."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**When to use gradient checking:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Situation | Do gradient check? |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----------|-------------------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Adding a new operation to your autograd | Yes, always |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Debugging a training loop that won't converge | Yes, check gradients first |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Production training | No, too slow (2x forward passes per parameter) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Unit tests for autograd code | Yes, automate it |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Verify against manual calculation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x1 = Value(2.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x2 = Value(3.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "a = x1 * x2          # a = 6.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "b = a + Value(1.0)    # b = 7.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y = b.relu()          # y = 7.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"y = {y.data}\")          # 7.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"dy/dx1 = {x1.grad}\")   # 3.0 (= x2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"dy/dx2 = {x2.grad}\")   # 2.0 (= x1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Manual check: `y = relu(x1*x2 + 1)`. Since `x1*x2 + 1 = 7 > 0`, relu is identity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`dy/dx1 = x2 = 3`. `dy/dx2 = x1 = 2`. The engine matches."
      ]
    },
